Inside the loop, we first remove the front n-tersection from the queue, check if it is the ending n-tersection, and return "can be travelled" if it is. If the current n-tersection is not the ending n-tersection, we iterate through all adjacent n-tersections and add them to the queue and visited set if they are not already visited.

After the loop, if no path was found, we return "cannot be travelled". Otherwise, we return "can be travelled".

In the `getAdjacent` method, we create a new list to store the adjacent n-tersections of the given n-tersection. We iterate through all the valid paths and check if the current path contains the given n-tersection. If it does, we add its other n-tersection to the list. Finally, we return all the adjacent n-tersections as an array.

In the `pathContains` method, we check if a given path contains a given n-tersection by comparing all the vertices of the path with the corresponding vertices of the given n-tersection.

In the `getOther` method, we create a new n-tersection that contains the other end of the path that contains the given n-tersection. We do this by iterating through all the vertices of the path and keeping the ones that do not match the corresponding vertices of the given n-tersection. Finally, we return the new n-tersection.

public static String canTravelMaze(int n, int[] start, int[] end, int[][] paths) {
    // Initialize variables
    boolean[] visited = new boolean[n * n];
    int[][] directions = {{-1, 0}, {1, 0}, {0, -1}, {0, 1}};

    // Create a queue to perform BFS
    Queue<int[]> queue = new LinkedList<>();

    // Add the starting n-tersection to the queue
    start[0] = start[1] = 0;
    visited[start[0] * n + start[1]] = true;
    queue.add(start);

    // Perform BFS
    while (!queue.isEmpty()) {
        int[] curr = queue.poll();
        int[] next = new int[2];
        for (int[] direction : directions) {
            next[0] = curr[0] + direction[0];
            next[1] = curr[1] + direction[1];
            if (next[0] >= 0 && next[1] >= 0 && next[0] < n && next[1] < n && !visited[next[0] * n + next[1]]) {
                visited[next[0] * n + next[1]] = true;
                queue.add(next);
                if (Arrays.equals(end, next)) {
                    return "can be travelled";
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // Check if the ending n-tersection is unreachable
    if (!visited[end[0] * n + end[1]]) {
        return "cannot be travelled";
    }

    // Check if there are any available paths
    for (int[] path : paths) {
        if (path[0] == end[0] && path[1] == end[1] && path[2] == end[2]) {
            return "can be travelled";
        }
        if (path[2] == end[2] && path[3] == end[2] && path[4] == end[3]) {
            return "cannot be travelled";
        }
    }

    // If the ending n-tersection is reachable and there are no available paths, return "cannot be travelled"
    return "cannot be travelled";
}

